WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.553
Select an operating-system image that supports the accelerator and the intended framework.

00:00:04.553 --> 00:00:08.634
A provider image with validated drivers and CUDA can shorten setup,

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:11.974
but its versions still need to match the application.

00:00:11.974 --> 00:00:16.798
Verify the GPU at the operating-system level, then run a small framework operation.

00:00:16.798 --> 00:00:21.993
Detection alone does not prove that model inference or training will use acceleration correctly.

00:00:21.993 --> 00:00:24.219
Containers can package the application, libraries,

00:00:24.219 --> 00:00:28.672
and model server into a repeatable unit while relying on a compatible

00:00:28.672 --> 00:00:30.527
host driver and GPU runtime.

00:00:30.527 --> 00:00:33.496
Pin container images to known versions or digests.

00:00:33.496 --> 00:00:37.949
If using Python environments directly, isolate dependencies and record exact package versions.

00:00:37.949 --> 00:00:42.401
Notebooks are effective for exploration but should not become undocumented production servers.

00:00:42.401 --> 00:00:44.628
Secure SSH before beginning model work.

00:00:44.628 --> 00:00:48.338
Restrict source addresses, use managed or short-lived keys where possible,

00:00:48.338 --> 00:00:50.565
and remove default or stale credentials.

00:00:50.565 --> 00:00:53.533
Bind notebooks and model servers to private interfaces.

00:00:53.533 --> 00:00:59.099
Reach them through an authenticated gateway or secure tunnel rather than opening administrative ports broadly.

00:00:59.099 --> 00:01:03.923
Keep API keys and model-repository tokens out of scripts, notebooks, and machine images.

00:01:03.923 --> 00:01:09.118
Begin with a simple manual path: start the instance, verify acceleration, load one model,

00:01:09.118 --> 00:01:11.715
run one representative request, and shut down.

00:01:11.715 --> 00:01:15.055
Record commands, versions, ports, storage mounts, and expected output.

00:01:15.055 --> 00:01:16.910
Once the path is proven,

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:22.105
automate it with reviewed setup scripts or images and test on a fresh rental.

00:01:22.105 --> 00:01:27.300
Reproducible setup saves billable troubleshooting time and makes an instance replaceable instead of precious.
